@startuml class-core
title Core types and the extraction contract

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package proc_macro_flow_traits <<Frame>> {

  class "Extraction<T>" as Extraction {
    +value: Option<T>
    +reasons: Vec<Reason>
    --
    +value(T) / +failed(Reason)
    +with_reason(Reason)
    +is_failure() -> bool
    +absorb<U>(Extraction<U>) -> Option<U>
  }
  note right of Extraction
    A struct, NOT a typestate.
    A node can extract fine AND carry a
    complaint of its own — an unknown key
    is the PARENT failing to consume its
    input while the value stays good.
    Two states could not say that.
    (#cleanup)

    No lifetime: see Reason below.
  end note

  class "Extracted<T, I>" as Extracted {
    -extraction: Extraction<T>
    -source: I
    --
    +new(Extraction<T>, I)
    +source() -> &I
    +value() -> Option<&T>
    +reasons() -> &[Reason]
    +into_extraction() -> Extraction<T>
    +to_error(msg) -> syn::Error
  }
  note right of Extracted
    The extractor's OUTPUT and the processor's
    INPUT — handed over WHOLE, never unwrapped
    between stages.

    Source lives here, not behind ""T: Sourced"",
    because a FAILED extraction has no T to ask
    — the case a diagnostic needs most.
    (#extracted/source-when-absent)

    No lifetime parameter: ""I"" is always a
    borrowed node or a Copy wrapper over one,
    so it already carries 'ast.
  end note

  class Reason {
    +kind: ReasonKind
    -span: Option<Span>
    --
    +new(ReasonKind)
    +at(ReasonKind, &impl Spanned)
    +span() -> Option<Span>
    +to_error(&impl ToTokens, msg) -> syn::Error
  }
  note left of Reason
    Stores a **Span**; ""Extracted"" stores a
    **node**. Deliberate asymmetry:

    · a node is multi-token → needs
      ""new_spanned"" for its full range
    · a reason points at ONE token → needs
      no ""Span::join"", so it is exact

    ""None"" means "nothing finer than the node
    I sit on" and the renderer falls back to
    the chain. ""to_error"" takes that node as an
    ARGUMENT — a reason cannot render itself,
    because position belongs to where it SITS.
    (#reason/span-not-node)

    Span is Copy and owns nothing, which is
    why neither Reason nor Extraction has a
    lifetime. (#no-owned-nodes)
  end note

  enum ReasonKind {
    WrongShape
    UnknownKey
    Missing
    Duplicate
    Ambiguous
    Custom(String)
  }
  note bottom of ReasonKind
    CLOSED reasons, open rendering.
    Closed so the framework can interpret what
    it caught; ""Custom"" so an exotic grammar is
    never blocked.

    Three of these are now ALSO obtainable from
    rustc by re-emitting keys as a struct
    literal — see 09-diagnostics.
  end note

  interface "Sourced<'ast>" as Sourced {
    +type Source: ToTokens
    +source() -> &'ast Source
    +additional() -> &[&'ast Source]
  }
}

package proc_macro_flow_derive <<Frame>> {

  interface "Extractor<'ast, I: Visitable>" as Extractor {
    +type Output
    +extract_from(I) -> Self::Output
  }
  note right of Extractor
    Supertraits are the TWO QUESTIONS this
    stage exists to answer:
      ""Sourced""  = what is the source
      ""I: Visitable"" = how do we get there
    There is deliberately no third question
    about how to PARSE the node.

    ""Output"" is unbounded on purpose until
    Processor exists — the honest bound is
    "something the processor can consume".
    (#extractor/output-bound)

    Grammar types do NOT implement this.
    Reading a Meta into a ColourSetting is
    PROCESSING; putting it here was the
    stage-boundary violation that made
    Sourced look impossible to satisfy.
  end note

  interface "Validate<'ast, I>" as Validate {
    +type ValidityError
    +type Valid
    +validate(I) -> Result<Valid, ValidityError>
  }
  note bottom of Validate
    SURFACE-LEVEL ONLY: does this exist where
    required, is this within a bound. Never
    parsing, never grammar.

    Not vestigial — it was UNDEFINED, which is
    why every impl was ""Ok(input)"". The syntax
    stage now uses it for a real narrowing:
    ""Valid = (&Attribute, SyntaxHelper)"".
    (#pipeline/validity-scope)
  end note

  interface "Visitable<'ast>" as Visitable {
    +accept<V: Visit<'ast>>(self, &mut V)
  }
  note bottom of Visitable
    Implemented for the REFERENCE types
    (""&'ast syn::Attribute""), so ""self"" is
    already the ""&'ast T"" every ""visit_*"" wants.

    Implementing it for the OWNED type made the
    receiver unconstructible for value-passed
    wrappers — it needed a ""&'ast Self"" pointing
    at something built on the stack.
    (#visitable/by-value)
  end note

  class "extract / extract_each / extract_maybe" as FromHelpers <<(F,#FFCC88)>> {
    extract<T, I>(I) -> T::Output
    extract_each<T, I, N>(N) -> Vec<T::Output>
    extract_maybe<T, I>(Option<I>) -> Option<T::Output>
  }
  note bottom of FromHelpers
    What ""#[from = ..]"" lowers to. Which one a
    field uses is read off its TYPE, never off
    the attribute (#from/arity-from-type).

    Call sites must name T: ""T::Output"" is an
    associated type and so not injective.
    Generated code always knows it.
    (#from/names-its-target)
  end note
}

Extracted *-- Extraction
Extraction *-- "0..*" Reason
Reason *-- ReasonKind
Extractor --|> Sourced
Extractor --|> Validate
Extractor ..> Extracted : Output is\ntypically
FromHelpers ..> Extractor : drives

@enduml
